:"POLD2","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":8.36424e-24,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.107512,"nucleus_score":-10.1206,"pct_ad":0.212082,"pct_control":0.229563,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.970091,"donor_log2fc":-0.0168158,"donor_lfcse":0.119433,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00159901,"degas_log2fc":0.526413,"degas_padj":0.0},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"POLD2","gene_symbol_current":"POLD2","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":2.40444e-30,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.196134,"nucleus_score":-11.5649,"pct_ad":0.134799,"pct_control":0.154075,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.766198,"donor_log2fc":-0.134922,"donor_lfcse":0.113922,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00496847,"degas_log2fc":0.560209,"degas_padj":3.94247e-165},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_symbol":"POLD2","gene_symbol_current":"POLD2","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.868346,"donor_log2fc":-0.105403,"donor_lfcse":0.159679,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00836371,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"POLD2","gene_symbol_current":"POLD2","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.591537,"nucleus_log2fc":0.048145,"nucleus_score":0.774642,"pct_ad":0.162094,"pct_control":0.157155,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.0640307,"donor_lfcse":0.129953,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":3.95187e-06,"degas_log2fc":0.344469,"degas_padj":2.25401e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"POLD2","gene_symbol_current":"POLD2","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.969057,"donor_log2fc":0.0287021,"donor_lfcse":0.093997,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00332267,"degas_log2fc":0.139052,"degas_padj":0.000262807}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0584132,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0896485,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0829391,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000106628","entrez_id":["5425"],"uniprot":["P49005"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes the 50-kDa catalytic subunit of DNA polymerase delta. DNA polymerase delta possesses both polymerase and 3' to 5' exonuclease activity and plays a critical role in DNA replication and repair. The encoded protein is required for the stimulation of DNA polymerase delta activity by the processivity cofactor proliferating cell nuclear antigen (PCNA). Expression of this gene may be a marker for ovarian carcinomas. Alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding multiple isoforms have been observed for this gene, and a pseudogene of this gene is located on the long arm of chromosome 5. [provided by RefSeq, Mar 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P49005","text":"Accessory component of both the DNA polymerase delta complex and the DNA polymerase zeta complex (PubMed:17317665, PubMed:22801543, PubMed:24449906). As a component of the trimeric and tetrameric DNA polymerase delta complexes (Pol-delta3 and Pol-delta4, respectively), plays a role in high fidelity genome replication, including in lagging strand synthesis, and repair (PubMed:12403614, PubMed:16510448, PubMed:19074196, PubMed:20334433, PubMed:24035200). Pol-delta3 and Pol-delta4 are characterized by the absence or the presence of POLD4. They exhibit differences in catalytic activity. Most notably, Pol-delta3 shows higher proofreading activity than Pol-delta4 (PubMed:19074196, PubMed:20334433). Although both Pol-delta3 and Pol-delta4 process Okazaki fragments in vitro, Pol-delta3 may also be better suited to fulfill this task, exhibiting near-absence of strand displacement activity compared to Pol-delta4 and stalling on encounter with the 5'-blocking oligonucleotides. Pol-delta3 idling process may avoid the formation of a gap, while maintaining a nick that can be readily ligated (PubMed:24035200). Along with DNA polymerase kappa, DNA polymerase delta carries out approximately half of nucleotide excision repair (NER) synthesis following UV irradiation (PubMed:20227374). Under conditions of DNA replication stress, required for the repair of broken replication forks through break-induced replication (BIR) (PubMed:24310611). Involved in the translesion synthesis (TLS) of templates carrying O6-methylguanine or abasic sites performed by Pol-delta4, independently of DNA polymerase zeta (REV3L) or eta (POLH). Facilitates abasic site bypass by DNA polymerase delta by promoting extension from the nucleotide inserted opposite the lesion. Also involved in TLS as a component of the DNA polymerase zeta complex (PubMed:24449906). Along with POLD3, dramatically increases the efficiency and processivity of DNA synthesis of the DNA polymerase zeta complex compared to the minimal zeta complex, consisting of only REV3L and REV7 (PubMed:24449906)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}